  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "Producer boundary runs pre-export/export and toolkit/library/rust/target-objects, requires a real gkrust archive, and rejects an already-built host object or XUL. It preserves configured root.mk/root-deps.mk. It is not a finished C++/XUL boundary.",
      "refs": [
        "QA:pipeline.py:444-469",
        "QA:checkpoint.py:168-197"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "xpcshell is GeckoProgram(dependent), whose template links nspr, xul-real and mozglue; xul-real links static:xul and gkrust. Cocoa MacWebAppService.mm belongs to xul. XUL native dependencies remain even for a single version-comparator test.",
      "refs": [
        "js/xpconnect/shell/moz.build:5",
        "build/gecko_templates.mozbuild:24-40",
        "toolkit/library/build/moz.build:5-13",
        "widget/cocoa/moz.build:108,189-202"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "RecursiveMake emits root target dependencies for recursively linked libraries and target-objects, includes root-deps.mk from root.mk, and exposes compile targets at the root. mach -C . with an explicit graph node retains root dependency traversal; a subdirectory build and RECURSE_BASE_DIR filtering are not equivalent to that closure.",
      "refs": [
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py:1586-1610,989-999",
        "config/recurse.mk:69-79",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py:1453-1465"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "binaries runs install-manifests-binaries plus recurse_compile and, on macOS, recurse_tools. It compiles all native default roots; it is not an xpcshell-only dependency target. Both binaries/faster together are documented as incomplete relative to a vanilla build.",
      "refs": [
        "Makefile.in:57-61",
        "config/recurse.mk:37-46",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/build_commands.py:184-194",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py:788-833"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "Current QA smoke requires executable current-job Mach-O xpcshell and XUL inside the configured app bundle, imports preprocessed AppConstants.sys.mjs, and uses stock mach xpcshell-test. It runs compiled-debug, intentional failure, and the original upstream version-comparator with the original head. It already disclaims native authentication/browser chrome/product qualification.",
      "refs": [
        "QA:mozilla_harness_smoke.py:248-300",
        "QA:mozilla-smoke/positive/test_current_debug.js",
        "testing/xpcshell/mach_commands.py:221-234",
        "toolkit/modules/moz.build:255-261"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "The app bundle is assembled in tools from staged dist/bin assets, with xpcshell/XUL routed to Contents/MacOS and other resources to Contents/Resources. Its declared binary inputs include the browser executable and optional updater. Shell target alone therefore does not establish that the existing bundle-based smoke has all resources or auxiliary runtime programs. The stock harness also installs tests and can start its existing HTTP3 server.",
      "refs": [
        "browser/app/moz.build:74-105",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py:1995-2071",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/assemble_macos_bundle.py:55-83",
        "browser/app/macbuild/Contents/MacOS-files.in:24-25",
        "QA:mozilla_harness_smoke.py:250-255"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "FasterMake builds noncompiled install manifests and selected generated files; its mac default also calls app repackage when not in hybrid recursion. A normal non-artifact configure defaults to RecursiveMake plus FasterMake, rather than the artifact hybrid. The producer export boundary alone does not prove later misc-generated modules/bundle are complete.",
      "refs": [
        "moz.configure:645-672",
        "config/faster/rules.mk:8-19,37-56",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py:1798-1834",
        "toolkit/modules/moz.build:255-261",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py:1853-1886"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "The plan applies extra fixed patches. Among inspected target/bundle files, brandingFileIcon.patch appends icon definitions to browser/app/moz.build and moz.build.patch adds a pre-build XPCOM manifest directory; neither removes the quoted xpcshell/XUL dependency edge. Any route must use the actual restored generated graph, not assume the unconfigured graph is complete.",
      "refs": [
        ".github/patches/upstream/brandingFileIcon.patch",
        ".github/patches/upstream/moz.build.patch",
        ".github/assets/pre-build/moz.build:8-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "classification": "confirmed-source",
      "statement": "xul-gtest and its Rust library are default or nondefault depending on LINK_GTEST_DURING_COMPILE. Without the restored effective setting and graph it is invalid to claim a second gtest link/Rust build was present in run47 or that omitting it would save a particular time.",
      "refs": [
        "toolkit/library/gtest/moz.build:29-32",
        "toolkit/library/gtest/rust/moz.build:10-15",
        "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py:838-861"
      ]
    }
  ],
